  "summary": "Agents now span antibody design, drug discovery, lab operations and model auditing, while biosecurity red-teaming and benchmarks test their reliability.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is infrastructure for LLM agents acting on biological workflows, now paired with evaluation of their reliability and risk. Antibody-design benchmarking tests instruction-following with tools and design history, and an agentic optimizer is compared against Bayesian optimization. PharmAgents2 proposes end-to-end drug discovery with knowledge extraction, parallel agent scaling and a 121-question evaluation. AutoDNA is the physical-execution element: an AI-native lab running 11,000+ steps across 20+ instrument types for DNA synthesis, sequencing and storage. AutoSPECTRA uses coding agents to audit foundation-model generalizability, and Building Barricades red-teams agentic biosynthesis planning. Only AutoDNA is peer-reviewed; the others are preprints, so cross-system comparisons remain limited.",
